        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>1a. No, Pylons do not have a turn, so are not able to end their turn on a hazard space, thus immune.</p><p>1b. Player created hazards last until the card that created is removed.</p><p>2. Just the 1 movement, the character goes back to normal after that.</p><p>3.Yes they need LoS, unless otherwise stated.</p><p>4. In the setup, the last sentence. It has you make a pile of 5 Scenario Markers, at the end of every round you remove 1. After the last 1 is removed, the match ends.</p>",
